{"id": "EUVD-2026-76545", "enisaUuid": "d2d0871d-c891-34d4-b9ef-43529dd7b0a4", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsmb: client: fix OOB read/write from unvalidated DataOffset in coalesce_t2()\n\ncoalesce_t2() computes data pointers directly from server-supplied\nDataOffset fields with no validation against buffer bounds:\n\n  data_area_of_tgt = (char *)&pSMBt->hdr.Protocol +\n                     get_unaligned_le16(&pSMBt->t2_rsp.DataOffset);\n  data_area_of_src = (char *)&pSMBs->hdr.Protocol +\n                     get_unaligned_le16(&pSMBs->t2_rsp.DataOffset);\n  data_area_of_tgt += total_in_tgt;\n  ...\n  memcpy(data_area_of_tgt, data_area_of_src, total_in_src);\n\nA small DataOffset can push a pointer below the actual byte area,\noverwriting header fields; a large one can push it past the buffer\nend, causing out-of-bounds heap reads (source) or writes (target).\nThe BCC overflow guard does not prevent this: BCC reflects how much\ndata is present, while DataOffset controls where in the buffer it\nstarts.\n\nThe \"validate target area\" comment present since the function was\nfirst written in 2005 was a placeholder that was never implemented.\n\nAdd lower- and upper-bound checks for both data pointers before the\nmemcpy, and before any target header fields are modified.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:45:28", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:48:05", "baseScore": 9.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6eb70b78e48b0031bd1a05fe1b58959a48e87739", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/36d01415d881d5326a0dd3384f781cd7e69aff2d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/672cf86aa6aa0fb4012ce4c3b3498df42ad67a4e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/033bc80019f07d158630df4e69b19a49010f54f1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6343c1da561962688f203362d80d6a3bfa39fa1b"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-89633", "GHSA-6jcv-m8xc-577h"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.49, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0143ff0b-11df-3cf9-b9f8-a2ae267026f3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e4eb295d38b57f4d4b956942a48887eb252d97c6 <033bc80019f07d158630df4e69b19a49010f54f1"}, {"id": "17d142fd-d437-3952-bac3-d3bd1686afa9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e4eb295d38b57f4d4b956942a48887eb252d97c6 <6eb70b78e48b0031bd1a05fe1b58959a48e87739"}, {"id": "39d8ed7f-69b2-3fd7-a389-54671e9774c1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.12"}, {"id": "3f643b4f-22e2-35e8-a308-798057a27853", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "5805352b-e0fa-3c6b-a009-9e92e4843618", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e4eb295d38b57f4d4b956942a48887eb252d97c6 <6343c1da561962688f203362d80d6a3bfa39fa1b"}, {"id": "63751a9b-6057-338c-ba07-8e86e3c3f845", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "8177b72c-8108-37ca-896e-27a053f88d81", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "823ed710-5951-3123-9f37-48f04021bf4b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "93cc9261-7111-3ae6-ba71-10eb81119bee", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e4eb295d38b57f4d4b956942a48887eb252d97c6 <672cf86aa6aa0fb4012ce4c3b3498df42ad67a4e"}, {"id": "b8174fc6-bae1-3b8f-90a2-4be647d0ae9a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}, {"id": "e67ef48a-0fc8-3009-863a-578e4af77c5f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.51"}, {"id": "ec759e1e-0bb2-33ed-aef2-bdb1cfdb94c6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e4eb295d38b57f4d4b956942a48887eb252d97c6 <36d01415d881d5326a0dd3384f781cd7e69aff2d"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "bfbe9ece-0309-3ee0-8676-04fa0037adc8", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}